   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated multi-sector assistance to support vulnerable communities in drought affected areas in Guji Zone, Goro Dola Woreda, Oromia Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe project at hand is an Integrated Response aiming at sustaining livelihoods of
vulnerable households to strengthen their coping
capacities, mitigate food insecurity, securing safe drinking water supply and provide basic sanitation
and hygiene, to restore their livelihoods as well as combating Gender Based Violence (GBV). The suggested activities were identified in consultation with the zonal/woreda line offices and
are in line with the Ethiopia Humanitarian Fund (EHF) 2023 First Reserve&#xa0;Allocation Strategy Paper and the Ethiopia Humanitarian Response Plan 2023 and address therefore the following key
elements:
1) Agriculture: Provision of crop and vegetable&#xa0;seeds (haricot beans,&#xa0;tomato, onion
and cabbage) Restocking of core breeding animals (goats and sheep) Animal vaccination campaigns&#xa0;Provision of
multi-purpose cash.
2) WASH: Rehabilitation and maintenance of water points Provision/distribution of essential&#xa0;water treatment chemicals (especially linked with the Cholera outbreak) Sanitation and hygiene promotion. 3)&#xa0;Protection: The project will address protection issues by providing&#xa0;GBV prevention and response trainings, awareness
creation on GBV to community, women and girls friendly spaces (WGFS),&#xa0;creating referral linkages and provide support to GBV survivors for psycho-social and
medical services. The project will address cross cutting issues such as GBV, PSEA, and disability inclusiveness as well.&#xa0;The project will be implemented by Caritas Switzerland (CACH),&#xa0;its national implementing partner
ACORD Ethiopia and Swiss Church Aid (HEKS/EPER)&#xa0;for a period of 10 months from August 2023 until June&#xa0;2024.lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
